OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F303A1786963675
OL,3,CEbola outbreak in DR Congo now
OL,4,Cdeadliest in country's history
OL,6,FYears of conflict and a highly mobile
OL,7,Fpopulation are making the 17th spread
OL,8,Fof the disease to hit DR Congo since
OL,9,FEbola was discovered 50 years ago even
OL,10,Fworse.
OL,12,FThere are no approved vaccines or
OL,13,Ftreatments for the Bundibugyo species,
OL,14,Falthough trials are under way,
OL,15,Fincluding one based on technology used
OL,16,Fto develop the AstraZeneca Covid-19
OL,17,Fvaccine.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G6/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,304,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30307
SC,0007
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F303A1786963675
OL,3,CEbola outbreak in DR Congo now
OL,4,Cdeadliest in country's history
OL,6,FStrikes by some unpaid health workers,
OL,7,Fthreats by rebel groups, anger from
OL,8,Flong-traumatised communities and
OL,9,Fmisinformation asserting that Ebola
OL,10,Fisn't real have significantly hindered
OL,11,Fthe response.
OL,13,FThe gaps are especially consequential
OL,14,Fin Nizi, one of the most affected
OL,15,Fhealth zones in Ituri, which accounts
OL,16,Ffor about 90 per cent of Congo's Ebola
OL,17,Fcases and four in five deaths.
OL,19,FViolence affecting the Ebola response
OL,20,Fhas also come from residents.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G7/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
